    "description": "Mineral Specimen Collection - Mixed Lot\nQuartz, Calcite, and Various Natural Stones\nNatural Geological Specimens\nThis collection features a variety of natural geological specimens, anchored by a significant large white geode with a visible crystalline interior. These pieces offer a range of textures, from raw, jagged mineral clusters to smooth tumbled accent stones, making them ideal for display, geological study, or as a foundational set for a mineral collection. The diverse array of colors and formations provides a comprehensive look at common mineral structures including druzy quartz and calcite cleavage planes.\nPieces Included:\nLarge white quartz geode, approximately 6.5 inches tall with hollow crystalline center\nMedium raw mineral specimens (2) featuring layered crystal structures and earthy inclusions\nYellow raw and tumbled stones (4) with vibrant saturation\nGreen tumbled stone (1) with semi-translucent appearance\nClear and smoky mineral accent pieces (multiple) in various sizes\nWhite flat mineral slab (1) with matte finish\nCondition:\nNatural geological specimens in raw and tumbled states. The large geode is intact as a specimen half with well-defined internal crystals. Smaller pieces show typical natural variations, inclusions, and fractures inherent to mineral formations. No significant modern damage beyond natural extraction characteristics. Total collection weight is 5.14 pounds.\nWarehouse Location: Cleveland\nDue to our lighting, white glare lines may appear on items - This is NOT damage\nIf you have any questions regarding the quality or authenticity of this item or general questions regarding and item, please click Contact Seller on the item page and send us a message. We are available to answer your questions Monday through Friday, 8 am - 3:00 pm, EST.\n* For combined shipping policy see the shipping tab.\nSome items may contain unseen flaws not noted in the description.\nSee Photos. Items sold as-is.",
